<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hòa Hảo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1939</span> · Also known as Hoa Hao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hòa Hảo is a Vietnamese Buddhist reform movement founded in 1939 by Huỳnh Phú Sổ in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-delta">Mekong Delta</a> village of Hòa Hảo. It stresses simple lay devotion over temples and clergy and quickly won a mass peasant following. In the 1940s and 1950s it had its own armed forces, fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> and later Ngô Đình Diệm's government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hoa-hao.jpg" alt="Hòa Hảo" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ban Trị sự Trung ương Giáo hội Phật giáo Hòa Hảo (Hòa Hảo Buddhist Sangha's Central Administrative Committee) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_H%C3%B2a_H%E1%BA%A3o.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
